    "lawCode": "Add §404-y, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5431\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to distinctive \"Appalachian Trail\" license plates\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nEstablishes distinctive \"Appalachian Trail\" license plates.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1-2: Amends the Vehicle and Traffic law by adding a new\nsection 404-y to create a distinctive \"Appalachian Trail\" license\nplate.\n\nSection 3: Effective Date\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Appalachian Trail is a marked footpath which measures roughly\n2,180 miles in length and travels through fourteen states. The\nAppalachian Trail's southern terminus is located in Georgia, while its\nnorthern terminus is in Maine. Approximately 88.4 miles of the trail\nruns through New York.\n\nThere are currently four states which issue special license plates for\nthe Appalachian Trail as a way to support the Appalachian Trail\nConservancy. This legislation would create a similar distinctive\nlicense plate in New York. These plates will be a great way for New\nYorkers to show their appreciation of the Appalachian Trail and\nAppalachian Trail Conservancy.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall become a law.\n",
